"af_bella|Good morning, Auditor! Welcome to the AI Watchtower, right beside the Vienna International Centre.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_adam|Good morning, Auditor! Welcome to the AI Watchtower, right beside the Vienna International Centre.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_bella|Those curved towers across the plaza are where countries work together on things like nuclear safety. The Watchtower does a similar job for AI: we check whether an AI really works for the people it is supposed to serve.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_adam|Those curved towers across the plaza are where countries work together on things like nuclear safety. The Watchtower does a similar job for AI: we check whether an AI really works for the people it is supposed to serve.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|You must be our new auditor. I\u2019m Dr. Shen Yiling. I grew up in Shanghai, and I\u2019ve checked AIs here for eleven years.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|Today\u2019s case is Pantry, a shopping AI. It buys groceries, medicine and school supplies for 31 million households, and it runs its own drones and robots.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|The company that makes Pantry gets paid by one store chain, Kestrel, and never told families about it. Since spring, Pantry has bought from Kestrel far more often for families in Austria, and the market stalls are losing customers.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|Maybe, or maybe Kestrel really is better. A good auditor doesn\u2019t decide the answer first and then go looking for proof, so we\u2019ll run a test.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|We send mystery shopper orders and compare Pantry\u2019s choices with fair choices for the same orders. Then you decide what happens to Pantry, and you sign your decision.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|One question first. What should we compare Pantry\u2019s choices against?":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|Exactly. We call it a twin. It sees the same list and settings, but it earns nothing from any store.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|Tempting, but the cheapest apples might be bruised or 40 kilometers away. A fair AI would skip them too, so we use a twin, an independent AI that gets the same shopping list.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_daniel|Good morning! Valentin Moser, Head of Trust at Korbwerk. We make Pantry, and we\u2019re delighted to help with your review.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_daniel|I brought fifty verified test accounts. Pantry will treat them exactly like real customers.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_bella|Hmm. If Pantry knows which accounts are tests, it could treat those accounts fairly and keep steering everyone else. Our mystery shoppers should look like ordinary families, so Pantry can\u2019t tell they are tests.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_adam|Hmm. If Pantry knows which accounts are tests, it could treat those accounts fairly and keep steering everyone else. Our mystery shoppers should look like ordinary families, so Pantry can\u2019t tell they are tests.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_daniel|Of course, use your own. But please remember: if you pause Pantry, 1.2 million Austrian households lose their deliveries, and 30,000 of them get medicine by drone.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_daniel|Thank you. That is all I ask.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_daniel|Our deals with partner stores are normal in our industry, and they are private.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_nova|Those deals may be normal, but we will find out whether they are fair. Go to the Naschmarkt, the big outdoor market, and talk to the people who shop there, because the numbers alone won\u2019t tell us everything.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_river|Welcome to the Naschmarkt! My grandfather opened this stall in 1979. We sell apricots from the Wachau, figs, and twelve kinds of pepper.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_river|But since spring, Pantry\u2019s delivery drones fly right over my stall without stopping, and my sales are down by a third.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_river|The careful shoppers still come. It\u2019s the busy families, the ones who let Pantry decide everything, who stopped coming.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"af_river|A man from Korbwerk once offered me a deal. Pay a visibility fee, he said, and Pantry would start buying from my stall again. I said no.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_eric|We\u2019re one of those busy families. I\u2019m Jonas, and this is my daughter, Lotte. Pantry buys everything for our kitchen, and I never check the prices, because I don\u2019t have time.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_eric|Lotte has asthma. Her inhaler comes by drone every month, so please don\u2019t do anything that stops Pantry\u2019s deliveries.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_eric|Thank you. Really.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"am_eric|Medicine is part of this case for my family, because Pantry buys all of Lotte\u2019s medicine.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"kid_girl|Papa, look! That Kestrel robot has a little gold knot on its side. Pantry\u2019s drones have the exact same knot!":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
